    "description": "Vintage Glass Insulators - 3 Pieces\nPressed Glass, Aqua and Clear\nVintage, Made in U.S.A.\nCollection of three vintage glass telephone or telegraph insulators, including one in a classic aqua blue-green and two in clear glass. These heavy industrial artifacts were a staple of early telecommunications infrastructure and have become popular collectibles due to their sculptural forms and light-refracting properties.\nPieces Included:\nAqua glass insulator, approximately 4 inches tall, beaded drip edge base, marked \"MADE IN U.S.A.\"\nClear glass insulator, approximately 4 inches tall, beaded drip edge base, marked \"MADE IN U.S.A.\"\nClear glass insulator, approximately 4 inches tall, smooth base rim, marked \"MADE IN U.S.A.\"\nCondition:\nOverall good vintage condition. All pieces show internal rust staining and surface accumulation within the threaded centers from former utility use. The glass remains structurally sound without major cracks. Minor fleabites, surface scuffs, or small chips common to salvaged glass insulators may be present. All markings are molded into the glass.\nWarehouse Location: Cleveland\nDue to our lighting, white glare lines may appear on items - This is NOT damage\nIf you have any questions regarding the quality or authenticity of this item or general questions regarding and item, please click Contact Seller on the item page and send us a message. We are available to answer your questions Monday through Friday, 8 am - 3:00 pm, EST.\n* For combined shipping policy see the shipping tab.\nSome items may contain unseen flaws not noted in the description.\nSee Photos. Items sold as-is.",
